course: dictionary
lesson: 8451
title: Words that name a place
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. Saharan is one of them. The word Sahara is a place name, and Saharan means belonging to or coming from that place. «Saharan silver ants come out at the hottest time of day» tells you these ants live in or come from the Sahara, a huge hot desert in North Africa.
explain: Context gives more clues. Words like hot, dry and desert around a word show you what it describes. «Saharan heat» means an extremely hot day, so Saharan can also describe weather or places that are very hot and dry, like the Sahara, even when you are not talking about the place itself.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Scientists put tiny stilts on Saharan desert ants» still makes sense if Saharan means from the Sahara. The word desert already tells you the place is dry and sandy, so the clues agree.
fact: Saharan means belonging to or coming from the Sahara.
fact: The Sahara is a huge, hot desert in North Africa.
fact: Saharan can also describe very hot and dry weather or places.
fact: «Saharan silver ants» come out at the hottest time of day, when the lizards that hunt them hide from the heat.
fact: A Saharan is a person who lives in the Sahara; this use is rare.
exercise: «Scientists put tiny stilts on Saharan desert ants.» Which place does Saharan point to? | The Atlantic Ocean | A forest in Scotland | The city of London | *The Sahara Desert in North Africa
exercise: «Saharan heat» on a summer day means what? | A quiet, dark night | *An extremely hot day | A rainy day in Scotland | A cold, snowy day
exercise: Which word in «Saharan silver ants come out at the hottest time of day» tells you where the ants come from? | time | *Saharan | hottest | silver
test: Which description fits the places where Saharan desert ants live? | Icy and frozen | *Hot, dry and sandy | Wet and green | Dark and underground
test: In «A Saharan is a person who lives in the Sahara», what does Saharan name? | A camel | *A person who lives in the Sahara | A desert storm | A type of cold weather
exam: Which sentence uses Saharan to mean very hot and dry? | «The Saharan rain fell all night and flooded the road.» | «The Saharan library is open on Sundays.» | *«The Saharan heat made us drink water all afternoon.» | «We went to the swimming pool on a cool, rainy day.»
